# Rust Workflow

- Use the latest stable Rust toolchain unless a crate or target requires otherwise. UniFFI bindings dictate the minimum version when active.
- Prefer `cargo add` for new dependencies so versions come from the registry instead of guesses.
- Write tests before implementation for ZK circuits, PQC vault behavior, and cross-language interop vectors.
- Run `cargo fmt --all` and `cargo test` inside `oss/crypto-core` after substantive Rust changes.
- For production code, add `cargo clippy --all-targets -D warnings` once the clippy component is installed.
- Keep `oss/crypto-core` independent from any unaudited helper crates. Production crypto must use audited or NIST-aligned crates only.
- Regenerate UniFFI bindings (Kotlin/Swift) in the same milestone that changes the Rust API, and run mobile tests to confirm the bridge.
- When a Rust-side change touches the wire shape with the Go backend, regenerate or update interop vectors and re-run Go tests.
